{"text": "\u201c= James Peet\n\nCc 808F\u2122Ft\u2014\u2122Y E-mail: RPeet@CPS.edu\n\nPROFILE: | am a school leader who values cultural and intellectual diversity and is driven to provide high\nquality learning experiences for all students. I strive to create mission driven, data informed and solution-\noriented systems of change. By working together, I believe schools and communities can create safe and healthy\nenvironments that foster social emotional and intellectual development for children.\n\nEXPERIENCE\n\nHernandez Middle School-Chicago, Illinois July 2017-Present\nAssistant Principal\n\nLeadership Development\ne\u00a2 Co-Lead Instructional Leadership Team\no Created and successfully implemented a cycle of professional learning around targeting teacher\npractices of increasing Agency, Authority, and Identity in the classroom\no Supported leadership development of ILT members - Created professional development around\ncompleting a walkthrough of the building; Created walkthrough protocols; Calibrated scores\nwith ILT members; Debriefed data to determine problems of practice\ne Created and Provided a Professional Development Series around Analyzing and Using Data\no Used flex day PD\u2019s to identify students underperforming on the NWEA or in class, based on data\nmeasures\ne Led Math Team\no Focused on alignment of standards - Reviewed yearly scope and sequence and began planning\nstages on redesigning pacing\no Coached teachers in implementing practices resulting in an increase of student centered learning\ne Co-Led CIWP Team During Writing Process\no Developed the sequence of activities that guided the CIWP writing team to on-time completion\nof the current iteration of the CIWP\n\nFamily and Community Outreach\ne Authored Grants\no Wrote and received a grant to partner with the Community School\u2019s Initiative, impacting 400\nstudents who have signed up for at least one after school program\no Wrote and received a grant to partner with the Dyson Foundation - Brought the Design, Build,\nTest Club to Hernandez\ne Developed School Partnerships\no Brought Becoming a Man to Hernandez to support our 7\" and 8\" grade boys in their social\nemotional development\ne Designed and Implemented after School Events for Parents and Community\no Partnered in organizing school events such as report card pick-up, school play, 6\"\"-8\" grade\norientations, press conferences, etc.\n\nInstructional Evaluation and Support\ne REACH Evaluation\no Successfully completed reach evaluation for 1/3\" of the teachers in Hernandez",
